cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pqtls-lab in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "pqtls-lab: a crypto-agile TLS 1.3 research prototype for measuring hybrid post-quantum key establishment"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-05
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nbermparis/pqtls-lab"

authors:
  - family-names: Bermparis
    given-names: Nikolaos

abstract: >-
  pqtls-lab is a research prototype implementing a TLS 1.3 client and server with
  selectable, explicitly defined key-establishment profiles, spanning classical
  elliptic-curve, hybrid post-quantum (ECDH combined with ML-KEM) and
  experimental standalone ML-KEM key exchange. It is built to measure the cost
  and reliability of migrating TLS to post-quantum key establishment: handshake
  latency, CPU and memory overhead, handshake size on the wire, and behaviour
  under emulated latency, packet loss and constrained path MTU.

  Its distinguishing property is that it fails closed and reports honestly. Each
  profile configures only the TLS groups it names, and the group that was
  actually negotiated is verified after every handshake on both peers, so a
  connection cannot silently complete over a weaker group than the one requested.
  Post-quantum key establishment, post-quantum authentication and symmetric
  record protection are tracked as three separate properties throughout the code,
  the metrics schema and the analysis tooling, so that a hybrid key exchange with
  a classical certificate is never reported as end-to-end quantum-safe.

  The project is a research prototype. It has not been independently audited and
  is not production software.

keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - TLS 1.3
  - ML-KEM
  - hybrid key exchange
  - crypto-agility
  - harvest-now-decrypt-later
  - network measurement
  - applied cryptography
  - secure systems engineering

references:
  - type: standard
    title: "FIPS 203: Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard"
    institution:
      name: National Institute of Standards and Technology
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      Standardises ML-KEM, the post-quantum key encapsulation mechanism used in
      this project's hybrid profiles. Note that the standardisation of the
      primitive is distinct from the in-progress specification work defining how
      it is carried inside TLS 1.3.

  - type: standard
    title: "FIPS 204: Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard"
    institution:
      name: National Institute of Standards and Technology
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      Standardises ML-DSA, used only in this project's experimental,
      capability-gated post-quantum authentication profile.

  - type: standard
    title: "RFC 8446: The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3"
    authors:
      - family-names: Rescorla
        given-names: Eric
    institution:
      name: Internet Engineering Task Force
    year: 2018
    url: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446"

  - type: software
    title: OpenSSL
    notes: >-
      Provides every cryptographic primitive and the TLS implementation. This
      project implements no cryptography of its own. Results are tied to the
      OpenSSL version that produced them; version 3.5 or newer is required for
      the post-quantum profiles.
    url: "https://www.openssl.org/"
